  "body": "﻿## What changed\n\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`: the existing `workflow_dispatch` gets an optional string input `app_run_id` (default empty).\n- When `site_only` is true and `app_run_id` is not empty, the `site` job does these steps:\n  - It checks that the id has only digits. Any other value stops the job.\n  - It downloads the `wasm-app` artifact of that run with `run-id: ${{ inputs.app_run_id }}` and `github-token: ${{ github.token }}`. This step has no `continue-on-error`.\n  - It runs `web/check-app-page.sh` on the download, and again on the copy at `app/`. On this path, a failed check is an error.\n- The `site` job gets the permission `actions: read`. It gets no other new permission.\n- The input goes into scripts only through `env:`. No `run:` script has `${{ inputs.* }}`.\n- `docs/decisions/3276-site-app-artifact.md` records the decision and the dropped options.\n\n## Why it is safe\n\n- No new trigger. The input is on the existing `workflow_dispatch`. Only a collaborator can start a dispatch, and a fork PR cannot start it.\n- `publish` is unchanged. A `site_only` run never publishes.\n- The tag path, a plain dispatch and a `site_only` dispatch without `app_run_id` keep their behaviour. On these paths the new steps are skipped, and `APP_RUN_ID` is empty in `env:`.\n- `actions: read` lets the job token read artifacts of this repository only. The job gets no write permission.\n- If the download or the page check fails, the `site` job fails and `pages` does not deploy. The deployed site stays as it is.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask --test release_site_tests`: 3 passed. The new test `site_only_dispatch_can_take_the_app_of_an_earlier_run` pins:\n  - the input, its type and its default;\n  - the `site` job permissions (`contents: read`, `actions: read`, nothing more);\n  - the two download steps (this run, unchanged; the earlier run, with `run-id`, `github-token` and no `continue-on-error`);\n  - the id check before the download;\n  - `web/check-app-page.sh` on the download, with an error on this path;\n  - no input interpolation in a `run:` script of the `site` job.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The existing tests `site_only_dispatch_runs_only_site_and_pages` and `the_site_job_runs_the_site_tests_with_its_pinned_zola` still pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No workflow ran. The real download of the artifact of run 44976953856 occurs only at the dispatch on `site/v0.25.0`.\n- No heavy lane: the diff touches only `release.yml`, an xtask test and a decision file.\n\n## After merge\n\nThe same `release.yml` is on `site/v0.25.0` as one commit (a dispatch uses the workflow file of the dispatched ref). The dispatch is:\n\n`gh workflow run release.yml --ref site/v0.25.0 -f site_only=true -f app_run_id=44976953856`\n\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #3276\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
